  "doc": {
    "description": "14 -- RingClock: a ring oscillator / delay line (requires N >= 2).\n\nThe unit-delay model gives every gate one cycle of propagation\ndelay, so a closed ring of N buffers circulates a pulse with period\nN (§11.2).  An OR gate with both inputs tied together is the idiom\nfor a buffer.  Drive `seed` high for one cycle to inject the pulse;\neach `out` bit then taps one stage of the ring.",
    "source": "circuit.shdl",
